    {
      "id": "doc-post-notes-on-slow-software",
      "kind": "post",
      "slug": "notes-on-slow-software",
      "title": "Notes on Slow Software",
      "description": "Small notes about software that values durability over novelty.",
      "date": "2026-08-04",
      "tags": [
        "software",
        "craft"
      ],
      "status": "published",
      "format": "mdx",
      "body": "# Notes on slow software\r\n\r\nSlow software does not mean software that feels sluggish. It means software whose design can survive a change in fashion.\r\n\r\n- Prefer plain formats.\r\n- Keep the publishing boundary visible.\r\n- Make upgrades deliberate.\r\n- Leave room for repair.",
      "sourceFormat": "mdx",
